      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression confirmed by live-cell anti-FLAG staining of non-permeabilized cells; channel trafficking to the plasma membrane was not disrupted. Electrophysiological function of the FLAG-tagged construct is not explicitly reported in the cited clip.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 explicitly names residues 307 and 308 as the junction in a full-length, membrane-anchored KV1.5 construct. Python lookup confirms residue 307 = P and residue 308 = S, both within the authoritative S1\u2013S2 extracellular loop (270\u2013322). The insertion sits 38 residues from the S1 TM boundary and 15 residues from the S2 TM boundary, satisfying the \u22653-residue clearance rule on both sides. The FLAG tag (8 aa) is shorter than the 13\u201323 aa ALFA-tag target but establishes that this loop tolerates an insertion at this exact junction. Full-length KV1.5 in a KV\u03b21.3\u2013IRES\u2013KV1.5 bicistronic construct; FLAG epitope inserted between residues 307 and 308 of the S1\u2013S2 extracellular loop by overlapping PCR. The tagged channel was expressed in mammalian cells and used for surface-trafficking studies.",
